Just a clarification about this failure:

This failure is due to this kernel patch "drm/xe/oa: Allow exec_queue's to
be specified only for OAG OA unit". This IGT patch will fix this failure:

"tests/intel/xe_oa: Drop oa-unit-exclusive-stream-exec-q". It is posted here:

https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/690390/?series=158083&rev=1

The kernel patch is needed. Without it, we will see a different failure
when we run the mmio trigger test on all OA units. Without the kernel patch
the following check will fail when we run the mmio_trigger test on the
OAM_SAG OA unit which does not have any hwe's:

static int xe_oa_assign_hwe(struct xe_oa *oa, struct xe_oa_open_param *param)
{
	/* When we have an exec_q, get hwe from the exec_q */
	if (param->exec_q) {
		param->hwe = xe_gt_hw_engine(param->exec_q->gt, param->exec_q->class,
					     param->engine_instance, true);
		if (!param->hwe || param->hwe->oa_unit != param->oa_unit)
			goto err;


Here the 'param->hwe->oa_unit != param->oa_unit' check will fail on the
OAM_SAG OA unit. The best way out of this seems to be restrict exec_queue's
only for the OAG unit.

Thanks.
--
Ashutosh


